<%# locals: (icon:, label:, money:, trend: nil, rate: nil, hint: nil) %>

<%# Three value types, one card. `money` is a Money, `trend` a Trend that
    carries its own colour and percentage, and `rate` a BigDecimal FRACTION
    where 0.21 means 21% -- a return, which is neither of the first two.
    Formatting it here rather than passing a string in keeps the registry free
    of presentation, the way every other figure on this page is handled.

    nil is a first-class outcome for `rate`, not an edge case: the returns
    contract suppresses a figure when a rate is missing (R13), when an account
    has fewer than two balance days (R15), and withholds the money-weighted
    return from a valuation-only scope (R16). All three arrive here as nil and
    must read as "no data" rather than as zero. %>

<div class="bg-container-inset rounded-lg p-4">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
    <%= icon(icon, size: "sm") %>
    <span class="text-sm text-secondary"><%= label %></span>
  </div>

  <% if !money.nil? %>
    <p class="text-xl font-semibold text-primary privacy-sensitive">
      <%= format_money(money) %>
    </p>
  <% elsif !rate.nil? %>
    <p class="text-xl font-semibold text-primary privacy-sensitive">
      <%= number_to_percentage(rate * 100, precision: 2) %>
    </p>
  <% elsif !trend.nil? %>
    <p class="text-xl font-semibold privacy-sensitive" style="color: <%= trend.color %>">
      <%= format_money(trend.value) %>
      <% unless trend.direction.flat? %>
        <span class="text-base font-normal">(<%= trend.percent_formatted %>)</span>
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="text-xl font-semibold text-secondary"><%= t("portfolios.kpi_row.no_data") %></p>
  <% end %>

  <% if hint.present? %>
    <p class="text-xs text-secondary mt-1"><%= hint %></p>
  <% end %>
</div>
